<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <a class="back-link" href="/sharp-end-exposure/">← Back to app</a>

  <div class="wordmark"><span>Sharp End</span> Exposure</div>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="updated">Beta · Last updated July 2026</div>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Note on this document:</strong> This Privacy Policy was drafted to meet a beta-launch deadline and has not yet been reviewed by an attorney. Straydog Labs intends to have it reviewed and may revise the wording — this is a text edit, not a rebuild of the app. If anything here is unclear, contact us at the address below.
  </div>

  <h2>1. What Data We Collect</h2>
  <p>Depending on how you use SEE, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information</strong> — if you create an account: your email address and, optionally, a display name.</li>
    <li><strong>Climb and session data</strong> — the climbs you name, grades, terrain, setting (indoor/outdoor), result, and the somatic check-in data you enter (breathing, gut sensation, body state, activation level).</li>
    <li><strong>Reflection and journal content</strong> — any free-text reflections, fall/backoff/send details, or journal entries you choose to write.</li>
    <li><strong>Device identifier</strong> — a randomly generated ID stored on your device, used to associate data with you if you use SEE without an account.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback you submit</strong> — anything you send us through the in-app feedback form.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect payment information — SEE has no paywall at this time.</p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
  <p>We use your data to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Operate the core features of the app — building your climb history, zone calculations, and progress views.</li>
    <li>Let you access, export, or delete your own data from your Profile.</li>
    <li>During this beta period, understand anonymized, aggregate usage patterns to improve the app (for example, understanding which features are used, not reading your individual private reflections for marketing purposes).</li>
    <li>Respond to feedback or support requests you send us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your data, and we do not share your individual data with gyms, coaches, or third parties without your separate, explicit opt-in.</p>

  <h2>3. Signed-In vs. Anonymous Use</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>If you...</th><th>Your data...</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Create an account</td><td>Is stored securely in our backend, tied to your account, and accessible across devices.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Use SEE without an account</td><td>Stays on this device only, tied to a local device identifier — we do not associate it with anything else.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
  <p>SEE's backend is built on <strong>Supabase</strong>, which provides authentication and database hosting with row-level security — meaning the backend itself enforces that your data is only readable and writable by you (or, for anonymous use, scoped to your device). We take reasonable measures to protect your data, but no system can be guaranteed 100% secure.</p>

  <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>You can, at any time, from your Profile:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> your full climb history and data.</li>
    <li><strong>Export</strong> your data as a CSV or JSON file, or as a printable PDF.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> your data or your account entirely.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you'd rather make these requests directly, contact us at the address below and we'll handle it manually.</p>

  <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>We use <strong>Supabase</strong> (database, authentication, and backend hosting) to run SEE. We use Google Fonts to load the app's typefaces. We do not use third-party advertising or analytics trackers.</p>

  <h2>7. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
  <p>SEE uses your browser's local storage (not tracking cookies) to remember things like whether you've completed onboarding, your device identifier if you're using SEE anonymously, and app preferences. This data stays on your device and is used only to make the app function correctly.</p>

  <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy as SEE develops, particularly during this beta period. Material changes will be reflected by an updated "last updated" date above.</p>

  <div class="contact">
    <strong style="color:var(--text);">Questions about your data, or want to make a request directly?</strong><br>
    Contact Straydog Labs at <a href="mailto:beta@straydoglabs.com">beta@straydoglabs.com</a>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
